---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const title = 'Wanderburg Unlock Conditions — Every Verified Unlock Chain (0.9.9 EA)';
const description =
  'How to unlock everything in Wanderburg EA: Front Cannon at side cannons 10, Arms at ram 10, Repair Crew at 100 health boxes, Companion at 120 walking enemies, Spiderberg at Golden Dunes’ four bosses — and why toast ≠ owned.';

const ogImage = 'https://wanderburgguide.site/images/modules/still-camp-shop.jpg';
const heroSrc = '/images/modules/still-camp-shop.jpg';

const chains = [
  { action: 'Side cannons → upgrade level 10', opens: 'Front Cannon (front slot)' },
  { action: 'Front Ram → upgrade level 10', opens: 'Arms' },
  { action: 'Archer crew → upgrade level 10', opens: 'Archer Tower (side slot)' },
  { action: 'Destroy 100 health boxes overall', opens: 'Repair Crew' },
  { action: 'Destroy 120 walking enemies overall', opens: 'Companion (back slot)' },
  { action: 'Clear Green Plains’ four bosses', opens: 'Golden Dunes land' },
  { action: 'Clear Golden Dunes’ four bosses', opens: 'Spiderberg unlock toast (then buy)' },
  { action: 'Consume 100 units in one run', opens: '500 silver quest lump' },
  { action: 'Consume 1,000 sheep overall', opens: '2,500 silver quest lump' },
];

const toc = [
  { href: '#key-takeaways', label: 'Key Takeaways' },
  { href: '#the-rule', label: 'The one rule: toast ≠ owned' },
  { href: '#chains', label: 'All verified unlock chains' },
  { href: '#silver-shop', label: 'The silver shop' },
  { href: '#buy-order', label: 'First-week buy order' },
  { href: '#vehicles', label: 'Vehicles' },
  { href: '#faq', label: 'FAQ' },
];
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} ogImage={ogImage} canonicalPath="/unlocks/">
  <div class="editorial-hero">
    <img
      src={heroSrc}
      alt="Wanderburg camp shop — unlocks are purchased with silver between runs"
      width="1920"
      height="1080"
      fetchpriority="high"
    />
  </div>

  <div class="editorial-layout">
    <article class="editorial-main">
      <h1>Unlock Conditions</h1>
      <p class="page-meta">Last Updated · Sep 13, 2026 · Early Access</p>
      <p class="editorial-intro">
        Every verified unlock in 0.9.9 EA on one page — the in-run chains, the lifetime counters, and the silver that
        actually buys them.
      </p>

      <section class="takeaways" id="key-takeaways" aria-labelledby="takeaways-heading">
        <h2 id="takeaways-heading">Key Takeaways</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Toast ≠ owned.</strong> An unlock toast only lets you <em>buy</em> the thing in the loadout — silver pays.</li>
          <li>Level-10 chains: <strong>side cannons → Front Cannon</strong>, <strong>ram → Arms</strong>, <strong>archer crew → Archer Tower</strong>.</li>
          <li>Lifetime counters: <strong>100 health boxes → Repair Crew</strong>, <strong>120 walking enemies → Companion</strong>.</li>
          <li>Golden Dunes’ four bosses → <strong>Spiderberg</strong>; Green Plains’ four → the next land.</li>
          <li>No verified shop price grid — the only card-still price we can read is Tankbert at 1,500 silver.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="guide-section" id="the-rule">
        <h2>The one rule: unlock toast ≠ owned</h2>
        <p>
          <strong>Answer:</strong> In Wanderburg EA, <strong>every unlock is two steps</strong>: the in-run condition
          produces an <strong>unlock toast</strong>, and the actual purchase happens <strong>between runs in the
          loadout</strong>, paid with <strong>silver</strong>. Same screen for modules, crew, vehicles, and captains.
        </p>
        <p>
          That’s why the standard loop is: clear bosses → Overtime for silver → cash out → buy the toast you’re holding.
          Don’t stack toasts you can’t afford — farm until the purchase is real
          (<a href="/silver-farming/">Silver farming</a>).
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="rankings-section" id="chains" aria-labelledby="chains-heading">
        <h2 id="chains-heading">All verified unlock chains</h2>
        <div class="table-wrap">
          <table>
            <thead>
              <tr>
                <th>Do this</th>
                <th>Opens</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              {chains.map((c) => (
                <tr>
                  <td>{c.action}</td>
                  <td><strong>{c.opens}</strong></td>
                </tr>
              ))}
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
        <p class="meta-note">
          Also buyable in the loadout once unlocked: Turret Layer, Side Ballista, Fire Crew, Side Barracks, Companion,
          Fire Mage. Slot notes: <a href="/best-modules/">Best modules</a>.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="guide-section" id="silver-shop">
        <h2>How do I unlock Companion (and other modules) in the shop?</h2>
        <p>
          <strong>Answer:</strong> Companion is the cleanest example of the two-step rule: destroy <strong>120 walking
          enemies overall</strong> (lifetime counter, multiple runs), receive the unlock toast, then buy Companion with
          silver in the loadout — and remember it needs a <strong>back slot</strong>, so skip Spiderberg that run.
        </p>
        <p>
          The shop shows kit text on each card (Racer Ruth and The Count are read aloud on tape; Tankbert’s card shows a
          1,500 silver price). What no tape or still has shown: a full price grid. We won’t invent one — treat any
          “complete price list” you see elsewhere as fiction.
        </p>
        <p>
          Silver sources, ranked: Overtime after a clean four-boss clear, quest lumps (the 500 / 2,500 silver counters
          above), then the end-of-run bank. Routes: <a href="/silver-farming/">Silver farming</a>.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="guide-section" id="buy-order">
        <h2>First-week buy order — what to unlock first</h2>
        <p>
          <strong>Answer:</strong> Buy the toast that extends the family you already run — for most players that’s
          <strong>Front Cannon</strong> first.
        </p>
        <div class="decision-tree">
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Front Cannon</strong> (side cannons 10) — biggest early power spike for the default kit.</li>
            <li><strong>Arms</strong> (ram 10) — if you’re on the ram / Overtime-mobility line.</li>
            <li><strong>Repair Crew</strong> (100 health boxes) — passive sustain that makes long Overtime sits safe.</li>
            <li><strong>Companion</strong> (120 walking enemies) — a real friendly unit, but only with a back slot free.</li>
            <li><strong>Captains</strong> — after the module core; pick by family (Pirate → cannons), not by vibes: <a href="/captains-tier-list/">honest captain comparison</a>.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="guide-section" id="vehicles">
        <h2>Vehicles — what’s verified</h2>
        <p>
          Vehicles live in the same between-run loadout. Verified so far: <strong>Spiderberg</strong> comes from
          Golden Dunes’ four bosses (toast, then buy) and has <strong>no back slot</strong> — it eats the slot Companion
          needs. <strong>Tankenburg</strong> (“Bulldoze everything!”) is the other named EA vehicle on the achievement
          list; its unlock condition isn’t readable on our tapes yet.
        </p>
        <p>
          Some hulls get <strong>two top slots</strong> — worth checking on any vehicle before you buy, because it
          doubles the mortar / turret line. Full boss-to-unlock chain: <a href="/bosses/">Bosses</a>.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="guide-section" id="faq">
        <h2>FAQ</h2>
        <h3>Why can’t I buy Front Cannon after the toast?</h3>
        <p>
          <strong>Answer:</strong> The toast only opens the purchase — you still need the silver. Farm Overtime after a
          clean boss clear, then buy. If the shop doesn’t show it at all, you’re on an older save — the toast fires
          again next time the condition completes.
        </p>
        <h3>Do unlock counters reset between runs?</h3>
        <p>
          <strong>Answer:</strong> “Overall” counters (health boxes, walking enemies, sheep consumed) are lifetime —
          they accumulate across runs. “In one run” counters (100 units for the 500-silver lump) must happen inside a
          single run.
        </p>
        <h3>What unlocks artifacts?</h3>
        <p>
          <strong>Answer:</strong> Artifacts are named in the official between-run unlocks, but we don’t yet have a
          verified unlock condition for a single artifact on EN tape — it’s the top entry on our still-checking list.
        </p>
      </section>

      <div class="crosslinks">
        <strong>Next:</strong>
        <a href="/best-modules/">Best modules</a> ·
        <a href="/bosses/">Bosses</a> ·
        <a href="/silver-farming/">Silver farming</a> ·
        <a href="/">Home</a>
      </div>

      <details class="still-checking">
        <summary>Still checking</summary>
        <ul>
          <li>Shop silver prices — only Tankbert’s 1,500 is card-verified.</li>
          <li>Tankenburg unlock condition; artifact unlock conditions.</li>
          <li>Exact slots for Cannon Tower / Force Mage.</li>
          <li>0.9.9 patch string not confirmed on Steam news.</li>
        </ul>
      </details>
    </article>

    <aside class="toc" aria-label="On this page">
      <p class="toc-label">On this page</p>
      <nav>
        {toc.map((item, i) => (
          <a href={item.href} class={i === 0 ? 'is-active' : undefined}>{item.label}</a>
        ))}
      </nav>
    </aside>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
